{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/16367-cyberpunk-werewolves","id":16367,"title":"Cyberpunk Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-22T17:55:35-08:00","id":16367,"title":"Cyberpunk Werewolves","content":"In a cyberpunk game which includes augmentations, what would be some possibilities with augs and werewolves? I'm thinking if the Rite of Dedication is cast on an augmentation (or cluster of them) then you can shift with them but normally with clothes and stuff like that they disappear when you shift. Though if it doesn't interrupt or interfere with your new form, it normally remains which is likely to be the case with most augments.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? How would you handle it? Would you allow or disallow augs?<br /> <br /> These are NPCs so game balance isn't something I need to worry about it. And I know every game's needs are different but I'm truly curious to see how other people would treat it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:59:47-08:00","id":16410,"title":"","content":"In a cyberpunk game, sure. I think it's covered in...Bleeding Edge? It's one of the Mirrors books, there's some cybernetic implant stuff there.<br /> <br /> Obviously the really boss werewolves would find ways to bind demons into their decks and fire off embeds when they need to. Boss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T06:32:30-08:00","id":19693,"title":"","content":"One idea is that you could have your augmentation crafted and then bind a spirit too it making it a fetish, then it would be functional whilst in a different form.<br /> <br /> I thought about this as an idea once and am really interested to see what people come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T12:39:49-08:00","id":20300,"title":"","content":"Cyberpunk Werewolves are an interesting premise. Will you just add Cyberpunk to the Core Game or do you change the background lore for this?<br /> (like making the werwolf origin scientific somehow, making the shadow to virtual reality or something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T13:43:49-08:00","id":20345,"title":"","content":"There's the Lodge of Wires, who have already embraced the idea of a cybernetic werewolf future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T13:53:17-08:00","id":20350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/16367-cyberpunk-werewolves?p=20345#post20345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the Lodge of Wires, who have already embraced the idea of a cybernetic werewolf future.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah??? which book ??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T13:56:04-08:00","id":20352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doc Lumbago</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/16367-cyberpunk-werewolves?p=20350#post20350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah??? which book ??</div> </div> </div> </div>Tribes of the Moon. They originally tried to bind the spirit of the internet, but it wiped them out. There's a new group, however, and they're pretty forward-thinking. I think their fetish is pretty useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T01:54:25-08:00","id":23016,"title":"","content":"In Bleeding Edge, the cyberpunk book for nwod, plug-ins are merits, and there is no functional difference between a handheld or worn plug-in and an implanted one.<br /> <br /> So balance wise, there's really no point in punishing a werewolf for getting cybereyes when they could just as easily wear cyber-sunglasses with the exact same effect, at the exact same cost.<br /> <br /> However, blood of the wolf indicates that for a werewolf to not heal an injury like losing an eye or a hand or whatever costs a willpower dot, so intrusive plug-ins like a cyberhand would be limited not only by the rite of dedication but how much willpower the character is willing to blow.<br /> <br /> Werewolves would probably be better of in a world with nanotech though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}